Parity reproduced VERBATIM from the web source (this is the spec, not a "corrected" version):
  • Sort: anomalies stably sorted ascending by SEVERITY_ORDER (critical 0 / warning 1 / info 2;
    unknown → 2). Stability pinned via the original index (web Array.sort is stable).
  • Tip title: `${signal ?? '—'} · z=${fmtNumber(z ?? 0, 1)} · ${formatRelativeTime(detected_at)}`.
  • formatRelativeTime buckets: <1m "Just now" · <60m "%dm ago" · <24h "%dh ago" · else "%dd ago"
    (localized; a missing timestamp shows "—" instead of the web's empty-string "NaNd ago").
  • severityIcon: critical → octagon (danger/red) · warning → triangle (warning/amber) · info →
    info.circle (info/blue).
  • Impact badge chain (reproduced exactly, incl. the latent quirk): SEVERITY_IMPACT (critical→high,
    warning→medium, info→low) → WidgetTipCards.impactBadgeMap (high→success, medium→warning,
    low→neutral). A critical anomaly therefore renders a GREEN "critical" chip — the web's actual
    output; documented in AnomalyImpact.badgeTone so it is not mistaken for a defect.
  • Compact badge: count via fmtInt; SEVERITY_BADGE[maxSeverity] (critical→danger, warning→warning,
    info→neutral); label "%lld active". Empty → "No anomalies".
  • Standard list caps at 3 (web WidgetTipCards maxTips = compact ? 1 : 3, compact=false → 3).
i18n keys from source: widget.anomalyDetector.title, .activeCount, .noAnomalies,
  .severity.{critical,warning,info} (+ .description from registry) — all resolved through the P1/S10
  facade; the view holds NO English literals.

